[{"id":"dead-order-checks","itemId":"board-checklist","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"After programming, LD4 stays dark, though your design passes its testbench. Put these checks in the order the build reaches them, from your desk to the board.","explanationHtml":"<p>The testbench runs before Vivado does anything. Synthesis writes its Utilization report before place and route can time the design. The bitstream step comes after routing, and it checks only that each port has a pin and a standard, so whether each pin is the right one is yours to check there. DONE can light only once the board is programmed. Checking in this order, each check rules out a whole stage.</p>","type":"order","steps":["Run the testbench with the parameters the board build uses.","Read the Utilization report that synthesis writes.","Read the timing summary that place and route writes.","Check every port's pin against the master XDC.","Program the board and check that DONE lights."],"shuffled":[3,2,0,4,1]},{"id":"dead-report-wns","itemId":"board-checklist","role":"core","promptHtml":"Your <code class=\"nobreak\">hello</code> passes <code class=\"nobreak\">hello_tb</code>, but on the board the terminal shows nothing. Below is the Design Timing Summary of the course's build of <code class=\"nobreak\">hello</code>, from the same code and constraints.","explanationHtml":"<p>5.778 ns to spare on the worst path, against the 10 ns clock the constraints file describes, and every constraint met. So timing is not why this <code class=\"nobreak\">hello</code> is silent: look further down the checklist, at the pins and at the terminal's settings.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/hello/arty-a7-100t/timing_summary.rpt","firstLine":139,"excerpt":["    WNS(ns)      TNS(ns)  TNS Failing Endpoints  TNS Total Endpoints      WHS(ns)      THS(ns)  THS Failing Endpoints  THS Total Endpoints     WPWS(ns)     TPWS(ns)  TPWS Failing Endpoints  TPWS Total Endpoints  ","    -------      -------  ---------------------  -------------------      -------      -------  ---------------------  -------------------     --------     --------  ----------------------  --------------------  ","      5.778        0.000                      0                   89        0.152        0.000                      0                   89        4.500        0.000                       0                    54  ","","","All user specified timing constraints are met."],"ask":"What WNS does the report give, in nanoseconds?","answer":"5.778","numeric":true,"unit":"ns"},{"id":"dead-find-bug","itemId":"board-checklist","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">tick_led_bug</code> should change LD4 every half second and keep it off while BTN0 is held down. Its author tested it with <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> held at 0 to reset it, and it passed. On the board LD4 never lights. Its testbench here drives <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> as BTN0 does, 1 only while pressed, and fails. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>if (~rst) led &lt;= 1'b0;</code> resets <code class=\"nobreak\">led</code> while <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is 0, which is all the time BTN0 is up, so LD4 is held dark. BTN0 reads 1 only while pressed, so the reset must test <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> itself, as <code class=\"nobreak\">tick_led</code> does. The author's testbench passed because it drove <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> the same wrong way the code expected.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-07/tick_led_bug/tick_led_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// LED led should change once in every LAST + 1 cycles of clk, as in","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// tick_led. rst is button BTN0, which reads 1 while it is pressed and 0","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// the rest of the time: holding BTN0 down should keep led off.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"tick_led_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"#","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"parameter","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"int","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"              BITS ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"26","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":",","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"parameter","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [BITS","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"-","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] LAST ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"49_999_999","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false}],[{"text":") (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold"